{"name":"Pacific Navy","hex":"#25488a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pacific","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Calm, peaceful.","Preferring peace by nature; avoiding violence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pacific"},{"term":"navy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A country's entire maritime military force, including ships and personnel.","A governmental department in charge of a country's maritime military force."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the dark blue colour of navy blue.","Belonging to the navy; typical of the navy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/navy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pacific Ocean","blocks":[{"text":"The Pacific Ocean is the largest and deepest of Earth's five oceanic divisions. It stretches from the Arctic Ocean in the north to the Southern Ocean, or, depending on the definition, to Antarctica in the south, and is bounded by the continents of Asia and Australia in the west and the Americas in the east."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/Pacific_Ocean_-_en.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacific_Ocean","wikidata":"Q98"},{"title":"Navy","blocks":[{"text":"A navy, naval force, military maritime fleet, war navy, or maritime force is the branch of a state's armed forces principally designated for naval and amphibious warfare; namely, lake-borne, riverine, littoral, or ocean-borne combat operations and related functions. It includes anything conducted by surface ships, amphibious ships, submarines, and seaborne aviation, as well as ancillary support, communications, training, and other fields."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/The_Hermione_being_escorted_by_the_USS_Mitscher_%28DDG-57%29_%281%29.jpg/330px-The_Hermione_being_escorted_by_the_USS_Mitscher_%28DDG-57%29_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navy","wikidata":"Q4508"},{"title":"Navy blue","blocks":[{"text":"Navy blue, also known simply as navy, is a dark shade of the color blue. The name navy blue originally referred to the color of uniforms worn by officers in the Royal Navy. In the late 18th century, the Royal Navy adopted the color for its sailors' uniforms, partly due to the practical reason that dark colors were less prone to showing dirt and wear during long sea voyages. The color became so associated with naval service that it came to be known simply as \"navy blue.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Flickr_-_Official_U.S._Navy_Imagery_-_The_Blue_Angels_fly_in_formation..jpg/330px-Flickr_-_Official_U.S._Navy_Imagery_-_The_Blue_Angels_fly_in_formation..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navy_blue","wikidata":"Q5975887"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Fijian_double_canoe%2C_model%2C_Otago_Museum%2C_2016-01-29.jpg/500px-Fijian_double_canoe%2C_model%2C_Otago_Museum%2C_2016-01-29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Fijian_double_canoe%2C_model%2C_Otago_Museum%2C_2016-01-29.jpg/1280px-Fijian_double_canoe%2C_model%2C_Otago_Museum%2C_2016-01-29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Fijian_double_canoe%2C_model%2C_Otago_Museum%2C_2016-01-29.jpg/500px-Fijian_double_canoe%2C_model%2C_Otago_Museum%2C_2016-01-29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Model of a Fijian drua, an example of an Austronesian vessel with a double-canoe (catamaran) hull and a crab claw sail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFijian_double_ca